          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Are cordless heated lunch boxes any good?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Most are disappointing. A battery small enough to fit in a lunch box stores little energy, so cordless models heat slowly and often leave food warm rather than hot, and their batteries wear out. A better approach is a preheated vacuum food jar, or a corded lunch box powered by a portable battery pack with an AC outlet or 12-volt port."
