        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is it safe to leave food in a heated lunch box all morning?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. Perishable food should not spend more than two hours between 40°F and 140°F, or one hour in hot weather above 90°F. Keep food cold in a fridge or cooler until about an hour before lunch, then heat it. Do not plug in a cold meal at the start of a shift and leave it warming until noon."
