            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "USDA guidance is to reheat leftovers to an internal temperature of 165°F. Some lunch box warmers bring food to a comfortable eating temperature that may fall short of that, especially with large or dense portions. Use an instant-read thermometer in the center of the food. If it is short, give it more time, stir if you can, or use a hotter appliance."
          }
