            3. The Five Heated Lunch Boxes Worth Buying
          </h2>

          <p>
            We picked these for real distribution, sensible power options and honest designs. We have not lab-tested them; specs come from the manufacturers' listings, and notes on heating behavior reflect what owners commonly report. Every one of them is slow compared with a microwave. The differences are in which outlet they use, how hot they get, how much food they hold and how easy they are to clean.
          </p>

