            Capacity matters more than people expect. A 20-ounce Lunch Crock holds about a generous bowl of soup or a modest serving of leftovers. Rigid 3-in-1 lunch boxes are typically sized for one meal with a separate compartment. HOTLOGIC's soft cases hold whatever flat-bottomed dish fits inside, and the Mini Max is sized for larger containers. If you eat big lunches or share, look at capacity before anything else.
          </p>

          <p>
            None of these is a microwave, and none of them heats in minutes. The fair way to compare them is by how well they fit your day: when you can plug in, how long before lunch, and how much food you need hot. The section on timing below turns that into a plan.
